    Harden session list/creation against async races and failures (R3, R5, R6, R8)
    
    - sessions controller: one createNew/remove transition is in flight at a
      time; the lock is acquired before the first await so a delayed mutation
      cannot overlap a send or a newer navigation. activate/createNew/remove/
      onSelect all check isTransitioning before proceeding.
    - refresh(): a generation counter plus query-equality guard drops stale
      responses; a recoverable HTTP error renders an error row via textContent
      instead of leaving the list blank.
    - init(): the search listener is attached before the first fetch so a
      keystroke cannot race the initial list.
    - pollForSessionTitle(): generation, session-identity, and query-equality
      guards stop a stale poll from overwriting a newer session's title.
    - api.js: listSessions throws on a non-OK response instead of silently
      returning null, so callers can render the failure.
    - app.js: bootstrap starts health, sessions, and history as independent
      void chains, so a rejected session fetch cannot block the badge.
    - INDEX docs: document isTransitioning, the transition-lock semantics, the
      search error path, and the poll staleness checks.
    - tests/test_frontend_bootstrap.py: source-level regression guard asserting
      the R1/R3/R4/R5/R6/R7 contracts against the shipped JS.
    
    Also updates the feature INDEX files to match the new contracts (R8).

